  <data name="Help_HowToUse_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>How to Use Masterwork</value></data>
  <data name="Help_HowToUse_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Masterwork plays community-authored scenarios for &lt;em&gt;My Father's Work&lt;/em&gt;. Start a module from "Start New Game," follow the passages as they're presented, and use the timeline scrubber to review — not undo — anything you've already decided.</value></data>
  <data name="Help_TimelineRewind_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Timeline and Rewind</value></data>
  <data name="Help_TimelineRewind_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stepping back lets you review what happened without changing it — links and inputs disable while you're looking at the past. "Resume from here" discards anything after the point you're viewing; "Return to present" just brings you back without discarding it.</value></data>
  <data name="Help_Saves_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Saves</value></data>
  <data name="Help_Saves_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each module keeps one autosave that updates as you play. Quitting from the in-game Options menu offers to save your progress under a name of your choosing before returning to the Continue list.</value></data>

